{{also|typ|тур}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|de}} {{m|la|typus||figure, pattern}}. Compare French {{m|fr|type||guy, bloke}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[tyːp]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Typ.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Typs|gen2=Typen}}

# [[type]]
#: ''Von diesem '''Typ''' Kaffeemaschine haben wir keine mehr auf Lager.''
# {{lb|de|colloquial}} [[guy]]
#: ''Schau dir mal den komischen '''Typ''' da drüben an!''
#: ''Der ist echt ein toller '''Typ'''!''

====Usage notes====
The weak declension (''dem Typen, den Typen'') occurs only in the colloquial meaning "guy", although strong declension (''dem Typ, den Typ'') is just as common. If the word means "type", it is always strong.

